{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetric","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicIsometryAffine","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Deriv"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.exists_horizTranslation_to_zAxis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.exists_horizTranslation_to_zAxis","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L199-L208","doc":"**WALL-2, one-point half (DERIVED).** Every point `p ∈ H³` is carried onto the\nz-axis point `(0,0,p_z)` by a horizontal translation, which preserves `dH`.  This\nis the elementary half of the normalization; the two-point reduction (bean\n`qou-0a0z`) additionally requires a boundary inversion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.zAxisShift_height","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.zAxisShift_height","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L194-L197","doc":"The horizontal displacement `zpt (p_z) − p` carrying `p` onto the z-axis is\nhorizontal (`_z = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pathLenH_vseg_eq_dH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pathLenH_vseg_eq_dH","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L177-L182","doc":"**The vertical segment is a length-minimiser** between two z-axis points: its\nhyperbolic length equals `dH (zpt a) (zpt b)`.  (Existence of a minimiser on the\nz-axis, DERIVED — the length equality is `pathLenH_vseg` matched to `dH_zpt`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dH_zpt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dH_zpt","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L169-L175","doc":"**WALL-3 (exact z-axis distance).** `dH (0,0,a) (0,0,b) = |log(b/a)|`, from the\nupper bound (`dH_zpt_le`, the vertical segment realises it) and the lower bound\n(`dH_zpt_ge`, the FTC vertical log-drop).  The 1-D core of geodesic uniqueness:\nthe vertical segment is a genuine length-minimiser between z-axis points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dH_zpt_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dH_zpt_ge","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L159-L167","doc":"**WALL-3 (lower bound).** Every admissible path between two z-axis points has\nhyperbolic length at least `|log(b/a)|`, so the distance is bounded below by it.\nDERIVED by specialising the unconditional vertical log-drop bound\n`dH_ge_logHeight` to the z-axis points, whose heights are exactly `a` and `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dH_zpt_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dH_zpt_le","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L151-L157","doc":"**WALL-3 (upper bound / existence).** The hyperbolic distance between two\nz-axis points is AT MOST `|log(b/a)|`, realised by the vertical segment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pathLenH_vseg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pathLenH_vseg","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L139-L149","doc":"**The vertical segment's hyperbolic length is exactly `|log b − log a|`.**  The\nintegrand is the constant speed `|log b − log a|`, and `volume (Icc 0 1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.admissiblePath_vseg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.admissiblePath_vseg","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L131-L137","doc":"**The vertical segment is an admissible path** from `(0,0,a)` to `(0,0,b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hypSpeed_vseg_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hypSpeed_vseg_eq","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L124-L129","doc":"**The vertical segment has constant hyperbolic speed** `|log b − log a|`: the\nheight factor `f(t)` cancels between `‖γ'‖` and `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.norm_deriv_vseg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.norm_deriv_vseg","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L118-L122","doc":"The Euclidean norm of the segment's velocity: `‖γ'(t)‖ = f(t)·|log b − log a|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.deriv_vseg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.deriv_vseg","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L113-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.differentiableAt_vseg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.differentiableAt_vseg","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L110-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_vseg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_vseg","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L101-L108","doc":"The derivative of the vertical segment: `γ'(t) = (0,0, f'(t))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vseg_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vseg_mem","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L98-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vseg_height","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vseg_height","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L95-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vseg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vseg_one","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L92-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vseg_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vseg_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L89-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.vseg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.vseg","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L85-L87","doc":"**The vertical z-axis segment** `γ(t) = (0,0, f(t))` from `(0,0,a)` to\n`(0,0,b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_heightProfile","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_heightProfile","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L78-L83","doc":"The derivative of the height profile: `f'(t) = (log b − log a)·f(t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_logInterp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hasDerivAt_logInterp","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L68-L76","doc":"The derivative of the log-interpolation exponent is the constant slope\n`log b − log a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heightProfile_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heightProfile_one","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L64-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heightProfile_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heightProfile_zero","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L61-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heightProfile_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heightProfile_pos","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.heightProfile","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.heightProfile","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L56-L57","doc":"The **height profile** `f(t) = exp(log a + t·(log b − log a)) = a·(b/a)^t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.logInterp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.logInterp","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L53-L54","doc":"The **log-interpolation exponent** `log a + t·(log b − log a)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.zpt_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.zpt_mem","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L50-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.zpt_height","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.zpt_height","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L47-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.zpt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.zpt","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L44-L45","doc":"A **z-axis point** `(0,0,a)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.single2CLM_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.single2CLM_apply","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.single2CLM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.single2CLM","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis.lean#L36-L40","doc":"**`single 2` as a continuous linear map** `ℝ →L[ℝ] E` — the injection of the\nheight coordinate into `H³`'s carrier, used to differentiate z-axis paths. ","signatureChunk":0}]}